; Independent review of neutral-symbol -> locale-recipe -> generated-surface.
; The Form-native review flow persists every answer before it is collected.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "cognition/form-neutral-word-field-locales.fk"
  "Review this Form-native locale realization seed adversarially and independently; do not edit any file. The primary object must be the numeric neutral symbol, with definition and 13-axis authored shape upstream; each German, Chinese, Portuguese, French, Indonesian, Balinese, or Sanskrit word must be generated by a locale recipe with only irreducible conventional spelling anchors held statically. Inspect every one of the 91 plans. Check Unicode, morphology, lexical category, register, and semantic fit, especially clarify, awe, sovereignty, grace, coherence, Balinese, and Sanskrit. Distinguish dynamic recipe interpretation from model-based generation and say if the implementation overstates either. Distinguish zero stored whole surfaces from still-static concept-to-fragment bridge choices. Treat all sense deltas as authored hypotheses, never empirical or universal language geometry. Verify that candidate/corpus/external evidence labels do not impersonate speaker review. Exact generated-surface reverse matching is only an identity witness, not general semantic understanding. The local band separately reports 32767 with 91/91 generated and exact round trips, 64 multi-fragment recipes, 19 body-corpus anchors, 3 external lexical anchors, and 69 authored candidates. Return PASS AS AN AUTHORED CANDIDATE LOCALE-REALIZATION SEED, REVISE, or BLOCK. Name every likely malformed or misleading surface, the strongest architecture correction, and the smallest coherent next implementation movement.")
